{# Commitizen's stock Markdown changelog template, with the commit link added.

   The only difference from the built-in template is the trailing link on each
   entry. Commitizen puts sha1, parents, author and author_email into every
   change alongside the parsed message, so reaching the commit needs no plugin
   and no Python - just this file and `template` in pyproject.toml.

   The repository URL is written out rather than passed through Commitizen's
   `extras`, because `[tool.commitizen.extras]` opens a TOML subtable: every
   bare key after it, changelog_start_rev and major_version_zero among them,
   would quietly become part of extras and stop being read.

   Pull request numbers are already in the text, carried over from the squashed
   pull request title. They are not links: GitHub only autolinks "#15" in
   issues, pull requests, commit messages and release bodies, never in a
   Markdown file rendered from the repository. See docs/releasing.md. #}
{% for entry in tree %}

## {{ entry.version }}{% if entry.date %} ({{ entry.date }}){% endif %}

{% for change_key, changes in entry.changes.items() %}

{% if change_key %}
### {{ change_key }}
{% endif %}

{% for change in changes %}
{% if change.scope %}
- **{{ change.scope }}**: {{ change.message }} ([{{ change.sha1[:7] }}](https://github.com/theadzik/workout/commit/{{ change.sha1 }}))
{% elif change.message %}
- {{ change.message }} ([{{ change.sha1[:7] }}](https://github.com/theadzik/workout/commit/{{ change.sha1 }}))
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
